# Collatz application

`research.collatz` is a **STRUCTURAL** application of `bt`, not the laboratory frontier.

- Do not claim a solution of the Collatz conjecture unless a matching
  `EXACT` statement exists; then state the theorem (quantifiers, Lean
  name, ledger tag), not the slogan.
- Use the seven ledger tags from `docs/README.md`. Do not write `PROVED` or `VERIFIED COMPUTATIONALLY`.
- New exact facts get a ledger row and a targeted note or test. Do not append a new numbered milestone by default.
- `C-T-welldefined` is Lean-verified in `formal/Problems/Collatz/Accelerated.lean` (`acceleratedT`).
- Import Collatz code from `research.collatz`, never a top-level `collatz` package.

Finite certificates, cycle searches, and range tables are `COMPUTATIONALLY VERIFIED` or `REFUTED`, never proofs of the conjecture.
